{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/261766-plot-seed-the-cipher-engine","id":261766,"title":"Plot Seed: The Cipher Engine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T21:31:35-07:00","id":261766,"title":"Plot Seed: The Cipher Engine","content":"This idea popped into my head, pretty much immediately, after I got Flower of Hell and hit the first mention of Lambdas, especially 2nd tier Lambdas.<br /> <br /> The Cipher Engine - A McGuffin - In which a surpassingly skilled Demon, having solved their Cipher, Installs the Embeds into four gadgets, then proceeds to assemble them into a third tier Lambda, recreating each of their interlocks on the way.<br /> <br /> The PCs may hear the story from an older more experienced demon, or from some information brokering other supernatural entity, they might discover the story in a Journal in an old abandoned bolt hole, from some system in a God Machine infrastructure, or even somehow recover the memory from an Angel during a Cover Jacking. Regardless, the tale is presented to them, as a guide to a supremely powerful artifact that might just grant them whatever they want (ok, it won't, but don't tell them).<br /> <br /> <br /> There was a Demon, an artificer of amazing skill, one of the first to discover that creating a Lambda was even possible. It is said that they cracked their cipher, and gained knowledge of how to attain their own personal hell. They set out to craft the Perfect Gadget. Taken in four parts, it was the workings of a simple Diesel Engine. Into the piston the first key was embeded, into the connecting rod the second, the third embed into the crankshaft and flywheel, and the last key into the engine body itself. After creating the four parts, they took them to their bolt hole, a heavily fortified secured location, warded in every way conceivable from the God Machine's prying eyes and Angels. It would not be enough protection to keep what was to come secret, but it would slow things down enough to give the needed time. The artisan then combine the components, one by one. Each Lambda was made to mimic the power of it's corresponding interlock, The first two parts created the first interlock, adding the crankshaft assembly created the Second interlock, and putting the whole together in the housing created the last, and completed the cipher once more. <br /> <br /> Another demon, the author of the tale, was drawn to the site by the STAGGERING aethric resonance. As he approached, the Artisan, in true form, cover shed, turned to looked at him and said &quot;To be free of the Machine, you must BECOME the Machine.&quot; And so saying, the demon reached out, and turned the manual crank to start the Cipher Engine. It turned over, and the piston fired, the motor spun up, and the Artisan faded from existence... The other demon fled, knowing this level of power output would draw the God Machine's attention. As he fled dozens, then hundreds, of angels passed him. Passed him unmolested, as if their business was to urgent to bother with him. As he watched, he saw the Angels could not approach the Engine. Could not harm it from afar. Could do nothing directly. The spread back out again, and he ran further still. A full twenty miles from the site, the angels spread out, forming a ring, then a dome, perhaps a sphere, for he could not say if there were angels under the earth or not. Joined into a phalanx of glowing energy, the horde of Angels excised that sphere, forty miles across, from reality, just to get rid of the engine...<br /> <br /> <br /> No one knows what happened to the Artisan, though many speculate. Some say he died, erased from reality by a catastrophic misfire. Some that he rejoined the God Machine on his own terms, perhaps even took it over, though if so his designs for reality are no kinder. Some say he passed into his own reality, one he controls as the God Machine controls this one. All that is known, if you believe the tale, is that a third tier Lambda is possible, and it's power is so great that the God Machine would sacrifice literally Thousands of angels just to take it off the playing field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T06:58:54-07:00","id":262111,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of the third-tier lambda being the combination of all of the Demon's cipher into a cipher-in-physical shape. Certainly food for thought!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:48:25-07:00","id":262677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/261766-plot-seed-the-cipher-engine#post261766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and said &quot;To be free of the Machine, you must BECOME the Machine.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! I might use that as a cypher any time soon. Great job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T09:02:57-07:00","id":267442,"title":"","content":"I likewise had the same idea of &quot;make a series of lambdas with your Keys&quot; when reading about the concept, though my take wasn't quite as apocalyptic or Cipher-sourced - I just figured it for the sort of thing a particularly introspective demon might do to gain insight into their personal mystical qualities.<br /> <br /> I do wonder about some alternative takeaways on the concept that might benefit from unique Interlocks, though - being able to incorporate form-gadgets into lambdas, for instance, or altering the way Living Installation works to allow the Unchained to &quot;breed&quot; a living lambda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}